language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Zebra puzzle: five houses in a row, numbered 0 to 4 from the left. Each house has one colour, one nationality, one pet, one drink and one job. Each entry gives the house of one item.
$ Index order: colours yellow, green, red, white, blue; nations italy, spain, japan, england, norway; pets cat, zebra, bear, snails, horse; drinks milk, water, tea, coffee, juice; jobs painter, sculptor, diplomat, pianist, doctor.
find colors : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(0..4)
find nations : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(0..4)
find pets : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(0..4)
find drinks : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(0..4)
find jobs : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(0..4)

branching on [colors, nations, pets, drinks, jobs]

such that
$ the inhabitants of the five houses have different colours
allDiff(colors),
$ the inhabitants have different nationalities
allDiff(nations),
$ the inhabitants have different pets
allDiff(pets),
$ the inhabitants drink different beverages
allDiff(drinks),
$ the inhabitants have different jobs
allDiff(jobs),
$ the painter owns the horse
jobs[1] = pets[5],
$ the diplomat drinks coffee
jobs[3] = drinks[4],
$ the one who drinks milk lives in the white house
drinks[1] = colors[4],
$ the Spaniard is a painter
nations[2] = jobs[1],
$ the Englishman lives in the red house
nations[4] = colors[3],
$ the snails are owned by the sculptor
pets[4] = jobs[2],
$ the green house is immediately on the left of the red one
colors[2] + 1 = colors[3],
$ the Norwegian lives immediately on the right of the blue house
nations[5] = colors[5] + 1,
$ the doctor drinks milk
jobs[5] = drinks[1],
$ the diplomat is Japanese
jobs[3] = nations[3],
$ the Norwegian owns the zebra
nations[5] = pets[2],
$ the green house is next to the white one
(colors[2] + 1 = colors[4] \/ colors[4] + 1 = colors[2]),
$ the horse is owned by the neighbour of the diplomat
(pets[5] + 1 = jobs[3] \/ jobs[3] + 1 = pets[5]),
$ the Italian lives in the red, white or green house
(nations[1] = colors[2] \/ nations[1] = colors[3] \/ nations[1] = colors[4])
